# Markdown feature gallery
	: fname=markdown.jpg notitle theme=github-light code_theme=default
	: root_symb=book root_sym1bf30
	: md md_width=260 mt1b
	: ## Root Markdown
	:
	: Each branch demonstrates a supported Markdown feature.
	: This introduction is itself a root Markdown body.
	# Headings and title colors
		: md mdw=420 mt[1,5]r mt[3-4]b mt5g
		: ### First title: red
		:
		: # Second title: red
		:
		: #### Third title: blue
		:
		: ## Fourth title: blue
		:
		: ##### Fifth title: green
		:
		: ###### Sixth title: default
		:
		: `mt[1,5]r` selects the first five titles; `mt[3-4]b` overrides titles 3-4;
		: `mt5g` makes the fifth green. Heading levels do not affect the count.
		:
		: **Bold**, *italic*, ~~strikethrough~~, `inline code`, and ==highlighting==.
		: Combinations: ***bold italic*** and ==highlighted **bold** text==.
		:
		: ---
		:
		: A paragraph can span
		: several source lines; with wrapping enabled, these are joined.
		:
		: This line ends with a backslash.\
		: This is a hard break.
		:
		: Two trailing spaces are an alternative hard-break syntax.
	# Bullet, numbered, and task lists
		: md mdw=380
		: * Star bullets use a dot.
		: * [x] Completed task keeps its bullet and checkbox.
		: * [ ] Pending task
		:   - A nested minus bullet
		:   - [x] Nested completed task
		:
		: - Minus bullets use a Unicode minus.
		: - [ ] A task with a minus marker
		:
		: + Plus bullets also use a dot.
		:
		: 3. Numbered lists preserve the starting number.
		: 4. Long list items wrap beneath the text, leaving the marker outside the continuation.
		:    * A nested bullet with **bold** text
		:    * Another nested item
	# List callouts
		: md mdw=400 cwhite fg="#202020"
		: * ! **Warning:** verify the backup before proceeding.
		:   This continuation shares the warning background.
		: * ? **Check:** confirm the configuration.
		: * $ **Success:** the deployment completed.
		: * @ **Info:** read the logs for details.
		:
		: * \! An escaped marker is ordinary text.
		: * `!` A marker inside inline code is literal.
	# Containers and nesting
		: md mdw=420
		: :::: note **Outer note**
		: Container titles support *inline formatting*.
		:
		: ::: tip
		: A nested tip with a ==highlighted detail==.
		: :::
		:
		: * [x] Review the nested message
		: ::::
		:
		: ::: warning Before deployment
		: Back up the configuration.
		: :::
		:
		: ::: danger Stop on errors
		: Do not continue after a failed verification.
		: :::
		:
		: ::: success Complete
		: The checks passed.
		: :::
		:
		: ::: custom Neutral container
		: Unknown container names use a neutral title background.
		: :::
	# Quotes and containers inside lists
		: md mdw=400 mt[1-2]p
		: > ## First nested title
		: >
		: > A quote containing **bold text** and a list:
		: >
		: > * First quoted item
		: > * Second quoted item
		:
		: - A list item containing a container:
		:
		:   ::: info Nested information
		:   ### Second nested title
		:
		:   Both nested titles participate in the node's title numbering.
		:   :::
		:
		: Setext heading
		: --------------
		:
		: Setext headings also render as Markdown titles.
	# Links and autolinks
		: md fontsans mdw=420
		: [Website](https://example.org) and [reference link][guide].
		:
		: HTTP autolink: <https://example.org/docs>.
		:
		: Local autolink: <file://filename.md>.
		:
		: [Local notes](file:///home/user/notes.md) and [local reference][notes].
		:
		: Links are styled text in the rendered image. File links do not load files.
		:
		: [guide]: https://spec.commonmark.org/
		: [notes]: file://filename.md
	# Tables with alignment
		: md fontsans mdw=440
		: | Left aligned | Centered | Right aligned |
		: | :--- | :---: | ---: |
		: | **Ready** | *Review* | 12 |
		: | `code` | ==Marked== | 345 |
		: | Long content can wrap within a cell. | [Link](https://example.org) | 6789 |
	# Local image
		: md noheader mdw=300 cwhite bw=1 bc="#64748b"
		: ## Embedded local image
		:
		: ![Outline rendering pipeline](assets/markdown-image.png)
		:
		: The path is relative to this `.otl` file. The image fits the available width.
	# Fenced and indented code
		: md mdw=440
		: ## Python with syntax highlighting
		:
		: ```python
		: # A comment is not an outline node.
		: def summarize(items):
		:     return {"count": len(items), "ready": True}
		: ```
		:
		: ```sh
		: python3 -m venv .venv
		: source .venv/bin/activate
		: ```
		:
		: An unknown fence language falls back to plain text:
		:
		: ```unknown-example-language
		: <literal text> & symbols
		: ```
		:
		: Indented code also renders as an image:
		:
		:     total = 1 + 2
		:     print(total)
	# Line and list spacing
		: md md_width=330 md_line_spacing=4 md_list_spacing=8 md_list_indent=30
		: This paragraph deliberately contains enough text to wrap into several lines,
		: so the additional spacing between lines is visible.
		:
		: * First item has an eight-point gap before the next item.
		: * The marker and its gap occupy the configured indentation.
		:   - Nested lists use the same indentation setting.
		:   - Another nested item
	# Compact spacing aliases
		: md mdw=330 mdlns=0 mdls=0 mdli=20
		: The short forms are `mdw`, `mdlns`, `mdls`, and `mdli`.
		: This paragraph wraps with no extra line gap.
		:
		: * Compact item
		: * Another item
		:   - Nested compact item
	# Preserve command newlines
		: md noheader fontmono mdw=160 md_wrap=off ctrans
		: #### Installation commands
		:
		: python3 -m venv .venv
		: source .venv/bin/activate
		: python3 -m pip install graphviz-mindmaps
		:
		: #### Verification
		:
		: python3 -m graphviz_mindmaps.cli --help
		: deactivate
		:
		: With md_wrap=off, source newlines survive and the longest line controls width.
	# Mermaid with theme color tokens
		: md noheader mdw=500 md_wrap=off ctrans fontsans
		: ## Deployment workflow
		:
		: ```mermaid
		: ---
		: config:
		:   flowchart:
		:     wrappingWidth: 1000
		: ---
		: flowchart LR
		:   A[Build] --> B[Test]
		:   B --> C{Passed?}
		:   C -->|Yes| D[Deploy]
		:   C -->|No| A
		:   style A fill:ccyan,stroke:cblue,stroke-width:2px
		:   classDef done fill:cgreen10,stroke:cgreen-10,color:cblack
		:   class D done
		:   linkStyle 3 stroke:cred-10,stroke-width:2px
		: ```
		:
		: The default `mermaid_font=on` passes this node's font and text size to Pele.
		: With `md_wrap=off`, the diagram keeps its natural dimensions.
	# Mermaid with Pele fonts and width fitting
		: md mdw=320 md_wrap=on mermaid_font=off
		: ```mermaid
		: sequenceDiagram
		:   Client->>API: Request
		:   API-->>Client: Response
		: ```
		:
		: `mermaid_font=off` uses Pele's font family; text size follows this node.
		: With wrapping enabled, diagrams fit the available Markdown width.
	# Svgbob inside a container
		: md noheader md_wrap=off ctrans svgbob_stroke_width=0.75
		: ::: info Local conversion
		: ```svgbob
		: +-------+     +-----+     +-----+
		: | ASCII |---->| SVG |---->| PNG |
		: +-------+     +-----+     +-----+
		: ```
		: :::
		:
		: `svgbob_stroke_width=0.75` gives thin lines; the default is `2`.
		: Svgbob uses a monospace font and this node's foreground color.
	# Svgbob with width fitting
		: md mdw=200 svgbob_stroke_width=4
		: ```svgbob
		: +---------+     +-----------+     +----------+
		: | Request |---->| Processor |---->| Response |
		: +---------+     +-----------+     +----------+
		: ```
		:
		: The image is fitted to `mdw`; strokes are scaled along with the image.
	# Literal markers and HTML
		: md rawmarkers mdw=420
		: The emoticons :-) and :-( stay literal with `rawmarkers`.
		:
		: * ! This stays an ordinary list item instead of a warning callout.
		:
		: Escaped markers: \=\=not highlighted\=\= and \*not italic\*.
		:
		: Inline code is literal: `==not highlighted==`, `:-)`, and `<b>text</b>`.
		:
		: <b>Raw HTML is displayed as text.</b>
		:
		: \::: info This escaped opener is not a container.
	# Emoticons and node styling
		: md noheader fontserif mdw=360 cteal fg="#202020" bw=1 bc="#64748b" bs=dashed symb=book
		: ## Body-only node with an icon
		:
		: Ordinary text emoticons become emoji: :-) ;-) :-( <3.
		:
		: The outline title is hidden; the icon remains visible.
		: Node colors, borders, and font attributes still apply to Markdown.
	# Outer title formatting
		: md hl1w2fmld mdw=320
		: The second word of the outer title uses a monospace bold header selector.
		:
		: Body formatting remains ordinary **Markdown**.
	# Ordinary sibling
		: node
